From 457711d34695c81d1e7849f021cfd42bfd90558e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raxcoms <mpaulo968@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 07:49:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] gamescope: connect the standalone Armada AutoHDR library

Supply device and game facts to the version 1 C API through a thin adapter.
The library owns inverse tone mapping, eligibility, presentation state and
pipeline retries. Gamescope keeps its frame resources and atomic commits.

Reuse the existing SDR gamut policy and LUT builder. A linear-color hook
runs before the shared gain, white balance and output encoding. One extra
LUT pair lets the game retain HDR while SDR overlays use standard tables.
Direct scanout and the normal composition fallback share that mapping.

The adapter uses the native presentation/allocation path when disabled,
with one cleanup when leaving AutoHDR. No extra GPU pass is introduced.
Update reviews must check the color-stage order, frame/layer contract,
shader slots and libliftoff call boundary.
